#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:-1
msgid "Overview of the text properties docker."
msgstr "介绍 Krita 的文本属性面板。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:10
msgid "Text"
msgstr "文本"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:15
msgid "Text Properties Docker"
msgstr "文本属性面板"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:17
msgid ""
"The :dfn:`Text Properties Docker` allows you to edit text properties of text "
"objects currently selected with either the :ref:`shape_selection_tool` or :"
"ref:`text_tool`. See :ref:`working_with_text` for an overview of all text "
"features."
msgstr ""
"文本属性面板用于编辑在 :ref:`shape_selection_tool` 或 :ref:`text_tool` 中选中"
"的矢量文本对象。有关所有文本功能的概述，请见 :ref:`working_with_text` 页面。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:19
msgid ""
"The docker has three tabs: :guilabel:`Paragraph`, :guilabel:`Character` and :"
"guilabel:`Preset`."
msgstr ""
"文本属性面板有三个标签页： :guilabel:`段落` 、 :guilabel:`字符` 和 :guilabel:"
"`预设` 。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:21
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Paragraph` will edit the default properties for the whole "
"paragraph, and contains both :ref:`text_paragraph_properties` and :ref:"
"`text_character_properties`. These can be edited with both tools."
msgstr ""
":guilabel:`段落` 标签页可以编辑整个文本段落的默认属性，包括 :ref:"
"`text_paragraph_properties` 和 :ref:`text_character_properties` 。这些属性在"
"使用形状选择工具和文本工具时均可编辑。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:23
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Character` will edit the properties for the selected word or "
"range and edits only :ref:`text_character_properties`. These are only "
"available when editing with the :ref:`text_tool`."
msgstr ""
":guilabel:`字符` 标签页可以编辑所选字符的 :ref:`text_character_properties` ，"
"这些属性仅在使用 :ref:`text_tool` 时才能编辑。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:25
msgid ""
"Finally, :guilabel:`Preset` allows you to create and apply style presets "
"onto the text. See :ref:`text_docker_style_presets` for more information."
msgstr ""
":guilabel:`预设` 标签页可以创建和应用文本样式预设。详情请见 :ref:"
"`text_docker_style_presets` 。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:27
msgid ""
"By default, the first two tabs will show only a handful of basic properties, "
"while all other properties are only shown when they are currently set, or :"
"ref:`inherited <text_inheritance>`."
msgstr ""
"默认情况下，前两个标签页仅显示少量基本属性，而所有其他属性仅在当前已设置或 :"
"ref:`被继承时 <text_inheritance>` 显示。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:29
msgid ""
"The revert button left of a given property will give an indicator of whether "
"a property is changed, and clicking it will undo said change. When a mixture "
"of style properties are selected, you will see a multi-headed arrow, while "
"the control itself will show the default or inherited value. Modifying the "
"control will set the same value on all properties, while clicking the revert "
"button will unset the property on all text."
msgstr ""
"每个属性左侧有一个“还原\"按钮，它们既可以反映该属性是否已被更改，点击它们还可"
"以撤销所做的更改。当选择了多个文本对象，而它们的同一属性有不同的值时，还原按"
"钮的箭头会从“单个”变成“多个”，而属性控件本身将显示默认值或继承值。此时调整该"
"属性后，所有选中文本的该属性将被设置为相同的值，而点击还原按钮将重置把它们全"
"部重置为默认值或继承的值。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:31
msgid ""
"New properties can be added with the :guilabel:`add property` drop down "
"below. The text input allows for searching the current text properties, with "
"each property having a number of alternate keywords. For example, typing "
"\"underline\" will list the :ref:`text_property_text_decoration`, which the :"
"guilabel:`Underline` option is part of. Selecting :guilabel:`Text "
"Decoration` will add the property to the list, so it can be set."
msgstr ""
"面板底部可以找到 :guilabel:`添加文本属性` 输入框/下拉菜单。在输入框中输入关键"
"词可以查找可添加的文本属性，每种属性都可以通过与之相关的多个关键词被找到。例"
"如查找“下划线”将列出 :ref:`text_property_text_decoration` ，该属性包含了 :"
"guilabel:`下划线` 选项。选择 :guilabel:`文本装饰` 将把该属性添加到面板中，以"
"便进行设置。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:33
msgid ""
"The visibility state of each property can be configured by pressing the :"
"guilabel:`configure button` next to the :guilabel:`add property` dropdown. "
"When the default visibility is set to \"always show\" and none of the "
"individual properties are set to show conditionally, the :guilabel:`add "
"property` dropdown is replaced with a filter input. The current visibility "
"states are possible:"
msgstr ""
"每个属性的显示/隐藏状态可通过点击 :guilabel:`添加文本属性` 下拉菜单旁边的 :"
"guilabel:`配置按钮` 进行配置。当默认显示状态设置为“始终显示”，且没有单一属性"
"被设置为按条件显示时， :guilabel:`添加文本属性` 下拉菜单将被替换为一个过滤输"
"入框。目前可用的显示状态有："

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:35
msgid "Follow Default"
msgstr "遵循默认配置"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:36
msgid ""
"The property will follow the default visibility state at the top of the "
"configuration window."
msgstr "属性将遵循配置窗口顶部的默认显示状态设置。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:37
msgid "Always Visible"
msgstr "始终显示"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:38
msgid "The property will always be visible."
msgstr "属性将始终显示。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:39
msgid "When Set"
msgstr "被设置过时显示"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:40
msgid "The property will be visible only when set."
msgstr "属性将只在被设置过时才显示。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:41
msgid "When Relevant"
msgstr "相关时显示"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:42
msgid "The property will be visible when it is set or when it is inherited."
msgstr "属性将在被设置过或被继承时显示。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:44
msgid "Never Show"
msgstr "始终隐藏"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:44
msgid "The property is never shown."
msgstr "属性将始终隐藏。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:49
msgid "Inheritance"
msgstr "属性继承"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:51
msgid ""
"Krita's text shape uses CSS, and thus allows for properties to be inherited. "
"This means that properties like the font size can be set over a whole text "
"shape, and ranges of text within the shape will default to the inherited "
"value if it is not explicitly set on the range."
msgstr ""
"Krita 的文本形状使用 CSS，因此允许属性继承。这意味着像字体大小这样的属性可以"
"在整段文本形状的级别上进行设置，而在此形状内部的部分文本除非进行明确设置，否"
"则将默认使用从整段文本中继承的属性。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:53
msgid ""
"Inheritance is useful because it allows us to only set the properties that "
"are important on a given section. So, we can emphasis a range of text with "
"italics in the :guilabel:`Character` tab, and then use the :guilabel:"
"`Paragraph` tab to change the font size or font family on the whole text "
"without losing the emphasis on the range of text."
msgstr ""
"属性继承让我们可避免重复设置属性。例如，我们可以在 :guilabel:`段落` 标签页中"
"统一设置整段文本的字体系列和大小，再在 :guilabel:`字符` 标签页中为选中文本单"
"独启用斜体以作强调。此后修改段落字体时，已设斜体的文本会自动继承新字体，仅保"
"留自身斜体样式，无需重新设置。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:55
msgid ""
"Conversely, some properties do not inherit at all, :ref:"
"`text_property_baseline_shift` for example. These properties usually get "
"added on top of one another, but the precise behaviour is described in their "
"entry."
msgstr ""
"某些属性不会发生继承，例如 :ref:`text_property_baseline_shift` 。这类属性通常"
"会相互叠加，其具体行为在后文中各个属性的具体介绍中有详细描述。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:60
msgid "Font-Relative Units"
msgstr "字体相对长度单位"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:62
msgid ""
"Some properties allow for font-relative units. The meaning of these units "
"also depend on inheritance mechanics. All font-relative units will try to "
"use the current font metrics. However, when said font metric is :guilabel:"
"`Em` and the property being edited is :ref:`text_property_font_size`, it "
"will be relative to the inherited font size. Similar with :guilabel:`Lh` "
"and :ref:`text_property_line_height`."
msgstr ""
"某些属性允许使用字体相对单位，这些单位的含义也取决于属性继承机制。所有字体相"
"对长度单位都将尝试使用当前字体的长度单位。但当所述单位为 :guilabel:`em` 且正"
"在编辑的属性为 :ref:`text_property_font_size` 时，此值将是相对于继承的字体大"
"小的单位——例如对于 16 pt 的字体，1 em = 1 个字身的大小 = 16 pt。与之类似的还"
"有单位 :guilabel:`lh` 用于 :ref:`text_property_line_height` 属性的场合等。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:64
msgid ""
"Font relative units are particularly useful for :ref:"
"`text_property_letter_spacing`, which is often done relative to the Em size. "
"Similarly, it is very common to have super scripted text to be set to 0.5 Em "
"(so it is half the regular font size), or to have :ref:`Shape Padding "
"<text_property_text_area>` to be 1 Ex."
msgstr ""
"字体相对长度单位对于 :ref:`text_property_letter_spacing` 特别有用，此属性通常"
"相对于 em 大小设置。与之类似的还有上标文本，它通常被设置为 0.5 em (即为正常字"
"体大小的一半)， :ref:`形状内边距 <text_property_text_area>` 则通常被设置为 1 "
"ex。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:66
msgid "Em"
msgstr "em"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:67
msgid ""
"The current font size (or inherited font size in the case of Font Size)."
msgstr ""
"数值上等于当前字体大小的相对单位 (当用于字体大小属性本身时，则表示继承的字体"
"大小)。其历史渊源为 M 字母的宽度。1 em 等于当前字体 1 个字符的点尺寸，如 16 "
"pt 的字体中 1 em = 16 pt。可理解为“字身单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:68
msgid "Ex"
msgstr "ex"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:69
msgid ""
"The current x height. This metric is retrieved from the font, and affected "
"by font size."
msgstr ""
"当前的 x 高度 (x height)。此长度单位来自字体，并受字体大小影响。其历史渊源是 "
"x 字母的高度，实际含义是小写字母高度。1 ex 等于 1 个小写字母高度。可理解为“小"
"写字母高度单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:70
msgid "Cap"
msgstr "cap"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:71
msgid ""
"The current capital height. This metric is retrieved from the font, and "
"affected by font size."
msgstr ""
"当前的大写字母高度 (capital height)。此长度单位来自字体，并受字体大小影响。1 "
"cap 等于 1 个大写字母高度。可理解为“大写字母高度单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:72
msgid "Lh"
msgstr "lh"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:73
msgid ""
"The line height. This is either relative to the current line height or, in "
"the case of :ref:`text_property_line_height`, the inherited line height."
msgstr ""
"行高 (line height)。这要么是相对于当前行高，要么在 :ref:"
"`text_property_line_height` 中是继承的行高。1 lh 等于 1 行的行高。可理解为“行"
"高单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:74
msgid "Ic"
msgstr "ic"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:75
msgid ""
"Relative to ideographic character :term:`Advance`. The advance of a single "
"CJK character."
msgstr ""
"CJK 表意文字的 :term:`字幅` (ideographic character)，1 ic 等于 1 个汉字的宽"
"度。可理解为“汉字宽度单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:77
msgid "Ch"
msgstr "ch"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:77
msgid ":term:`Advance` of the number '0'."
msgstr ""
"字符宽度 (character width)，1 ch 相当于 1 个字符的宽度，但在比例字体中，不同"
"字符宽度各异，因此 CSS 规范选择数字“0”的 :term:`字幅` 作为参考基准。可理解"
"为“字符宽度单位”或“零字符宽度单位”。"

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:82
msgid "Character Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:84
msgid ""
"Character properties are properties that can be applied on a range of text "
"or the whole paragraph."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:89
msgid "Font Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:91
msgid ""
"Font size allows setting the size of the characters. Particularly it scales "
"the whole font so that its design size (the \"em size\") is the same as the "
"font size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:93
msgid ""
"When using :ref:`font_relative_units`, font size will always use the "
"inherited font size and family as the reference font. This can be used to "
"ensure a range of the text is always a bit bigger or a bit smaller than the "
"surrounding text, which can be useful for superscript or titling."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:95
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:123
msgid "By default, this property is always visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:100
msgid "Font Size Adjust"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:102
msgid ""
"Font size adjust allows setting a ratio that the x-height must be matched "
"by. The x-height is the height of the small latin x in Latin fonts, and it "
"is a value that is derived from the font metrics."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:104
msgid ""
"This is particularly useful with font-fallback, but can also be useful in "
"general to force some consistency into the x-height. There’s a :guilabel:"
"`calculate` button, which allows you to calculate the font-size ratio of the "
"current font family."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:108
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/font-size-adjust-example.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:108
msgid ""
"Script fonts frequently have a much smaller x-height than typical body text "
"fonts. By using :guilabel:`Font Size Adjust` and pressing :guilabel:"
"`calculate`, we can set the text to have a similarly sized x-height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:113
msgid "Font Family"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:115
msgid ""
"Font family allows selecting a list of fonts that should be used for the "
"current text. The first item in the list is the primary font used, while "
"each subsequent font may be used as a fallback."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:119
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/font-selection-fallback-arabic.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:119
msgid ""
"Many fonts only have glyphs for a subset of unicode, so controlling fallback "
"can allow us to select fonts that seem to be in a similar tradition, like "
"using a Serif Latin font for a Naskh Arabic font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:121
msgid ""
"See :ref:`resource_fonts` for more information about the font picker and "
"font families."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:128
msgid "Font Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:130
msgid ""
"Font style allows setting the sub style of the given font family, such as "
"italics and bold."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:132
msgid ""
"The main control is a drop down that shows a list of predefined styles. "
"These are determined either by the fonts within a family, or by the "
"instances inside a :term:`Variable Font`. Clicking any of these will set the "
"corresponding CSS properties for that style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:136
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/font-style-examples.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:136
msgid ""
"The image above showcases a number of styles. The top row shows the effects "
"of width, weight and slant, while the bottom row shows the effect of "
"toggling optical size at different font sizes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:138
msgid "When unfolding this property, the following settings are available:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:140
msgid "Weight"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:141
msgid "This controls the thickness of the glyph outlines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:142
msgid "Synthesize Bold"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:143
msgid ""
"This allows synthesizing thick glyphs when there's no support for bold in "
"the font family."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:144
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:416
msgid "Width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:145
msgid ""
"This controls how much horizontal space a glyph takes. Not all fonts support "
"this, and there's no synthesis for this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:147
msgid ""
"This can be either :guilabel:`Normal`, :guilabel:`Italic` or :guilabel:"
"`Oblique`. The difference between Italic and Oblique is that the former "
"corresponds to a glyph style remniscent of the Italic calligraphy style, "
"while the latter is a slanted version of the normal glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:148
msgid "Slant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:149
msgid ""
"When :guilabel:`Oblique` is selected, the angle can also be configured. This "
"is primarily for use with variable fonts that support the slant axis."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:150
msgid "Synthesize Slant"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:151
msgid ""
"This allows synthesizing slanted glyphs where there's no italic or oblique "
"version of the glyphs available."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:153
msgid "Optical Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:153
msgid ""
"This determines whether the optical size axis in Variable Fonts will be "
"synced to the font size. Note that Krita interprets the axis value to be in "
"points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:155
msgid ""
"Finally, there's a place for the extra axes. These are for use with variable "
"fonts, which can provide more configuration for the font style."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:157
msgid "This property is, by default, always visible."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:162
msgid "Letter Spacing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:164
msgid ""
"Letter spacing controls the spacing between visible clusters of characters. "
"There are subtle differences in how letter spacing is implemented by "
"programs that support CSS. Krita's implementation follows CSS-Text-3 and "
"thus does not apply to single characters. Letter spacing is mostly intended "
"to apply to whole spans of characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:169
msgid "Word Spacing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:171
msgid ""
"Word spacing controls the size of word separator characters, such as the "
"space character. It also provides spacing for other word separator "
"characters, like the Ethiopian word space, Aegean word separators, Ugaric "
"word divider as well as Phoenician word separators."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:176
msgid "Line Height"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:178
msgid ""
"Line Height controls the line height used for the range of text. It does not "
"work for pre-positioned SVG 1.1 text, but does apply for pre-formatted text "
"that uses hard line breaks, or wrapped text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:180
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:336
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:343
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:350
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:372
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:399
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:444
msgid "Normal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:181
msgid ""
"When this is on, Krita will try to determine the line height by taking each "
"character in a line, and determining its ascent, descent, and also the line "
"gap metric. The maximum of these is used as the line height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:183
msgid "Ln"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:183
msgid ""
"Line Height has one unique unit: :guilabel:`Ln`, this is similar to \"normal"
"\", except it uses the font size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:185
msgid ""
"All other units will define a fixed offset. Even the :ref:"
"`font_relative_units` are fixed to the current font and size of the element "
"the line height is defined on."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:187
msgid ""
"When using relative units, Line Height will take the current font size and "
"family as reference. However, when using the line height unit, Line height "
"will use the inherited line height as reference."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:192
msgid "Line Break"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:194
msgid ""
"Line Break allows choosing a strictness for the line breaking algorithm. "
"Mostly used for CJK scripts, requires :ref:`text_property_language` being "
"set to work. Krita at this moment does not support :guilabel:`Loose`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:199
msgid "Word Break"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:201
msgid ""
"Word Break allows fine-tuning the line breaking by toggling whether to only "
"break at words or also allow breaking at characters. Useful for Korean or "
"Ethiopian."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:205
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/word-break-korean.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:205
msgid ""
"Krita slogan in Korean. On the left side there's the default behaviour, "
"which breaks after every hangul cluster. This looks rather old fashioned. By "
"setting word break to :guilabel:`Keep-all`, breaks will happen only at word "
"boundaries."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:210
msgid "Text Transform"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:212
msgid ""
"Text Transform allows transforming the given range of characters, for "
"example, by setting them uppercase, or switching out half-width forms for "
"full-width forms. This is useful in that it is applied as a stylistic "
"effect, meaning any text written is automatically transformed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:214
msgid ""
":guilabel:`Text Transform` is sensitive to the :ref:`text_property_language` "
"being set. For example, the Turkish undotted i will be transformed with the "
"I while regular i will be transformed to dotted I."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:216
msgid "Case"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:217
msgid ""
"Whether to transform all text to upper or lower case. In the case of :"
"guilabel:`Capitalize` the first letter after each word separator is "
"uppercased, which the rest is lowercased."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:218
msgid "Full-width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:219
msgid ""
"Full-width refers to the “Fullwidth” code points in the Halfwidth and "
"Fullwidth unicode block. Toggling this will mean that proportional or "
"halfwidth glyphs will be replaced with those fullwidth glyphs if possible. "
"Typically, in vertical text, proportional glyphs are rotated, but when this "
"isn’t possible or required, using full width glyphs can look a lot neater. "
"The full width opentype feature does something similar, but not every font "
"supports that."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:221
msgid "Full-size Kana"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:221
msgid ""
"In Japanese Kana scripts, there are some instances of small and big kana, "
"which have subtly different pronunciation. However, when the text is really "
"small, it can be useful to replace small kana with big kana to aid in "
"readability."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:226
msgid "Text Decoration"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:230
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/text-decoration-sample.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:230
msgid "Sample showing all the possible decorations as well as the line styles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:232
msgid ""
"Text Decoration allows drawing underlines, overlines and striking through "
"text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:234
msgid "Line:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:235
msgid ""
"Toggles whether underline, overline or line through is enabled. Multiple can "
"be enabled at once."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:236
msgid "Color:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:237
msgid ""
"Set the color of the underline. When unset, the color of the decoration will "
"follow the text color."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:239
msgid "Style:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:239
msgid ""
"The style of the lines. Shared between all enabled lines, these can be made "
"dashed, dotted, wavy and even double lines can be drawn."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:241
msgid ""
"Text Decoration does not inherit. Instead it is applied over each range of "
"text it is defined on, with later defined text decoration being drawn on top "
"of earlier defined text decoration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:245
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/text-decoration-nested.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:245
msgid ""
"Nested text decorations definitions. While something this complicated is "
"only possible with the SVG source editor, you can see a similar result if "
"you define a text decoration on the paragraph, and one on a range of "
"characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:250
msgid "Underline Position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:252
msgid "Specify the position of the underline for text-decoration."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:255
msgid "Behaviour in horizontal writing modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:257
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:653
msgid "Auto"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:258
msgid "Underlines will be positioned according to the metrics of the font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:259
msgid "Horizontal:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:259
msgid "Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:260
msgid "Underlines will be aligned to the descender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:262
msgid "Behaviour in vertical writing modes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:264
msgid "Vertical left"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:265
msgid ""
"Underlines will be at the left of the characters. Overlines at the right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:267
msgid "Vertical:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:267
msgid "Vertical right"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:267
msgid "Underlines will be at the right of the characters, and overlines left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:272
msgid "OpenType Features"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:274
msgid ""
"Some fonts include OpenType features like kerning, ligatures or small caps, "
"and can also involve a variety of alternative glyphs (or even contextual "
"glyphs) so that complex joined scripts render correctly. The latter type is "
"generally always enabled, and Krita provides control for the former."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:277
msgid "OpenType Feature Settings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:281
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype_features_ui.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:281
msgid ""
"Some features enabled in the medievalist font “Junicode”. The first four "
"letters are the \"OpenType feature tag\", which is the way these features "
"are stored in the font. The name can be retrieved from the font if defined, "
"otherwise Krita will provide its own name."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:283
msgid ""
"This provides precise control over Open Type features. OpenType features are "
"usually defined by tags, and whether they are on or off. The drop down will "
"provide a list of features in the primary font in the :ref:"
"`text_property_font_family` list."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:285
msgid ""
"For where it is feasible, a small preview is rendered, but for some features "
"it can be hard to provide this."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:287
msgid ""
"Typing in a feature name or tag into the search will show a filtered list of "
"all official features that match the search. This way, features that are not "
"in the primary font can still be selected and enabled (which is useful when "
"inheriting)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:289
msgid ""
"See also the :ref:`glyph_palette` for an alternate way of selecting glyph "
"alternates in the current text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:291
msgid ""
"OpenType features, while they inherit, inherit as one list. If you want to "
"give general hints for a given feature to be enabled over the whole text, "
"use the Glyph properties:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:296
msgid "Glyphs: Ligatures"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:297
msgid "Enable or disable ligatures and contextual alternates on the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:299
msgid "Common"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:300
msgid "Enables `liga` and `clig`, which are commonly used ligatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:301
msgid "Discretionary"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:302
msgid "Enables `dlig`, which are ligatures of a more decorative nature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:303
msgid "Historical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:304
msgid "Enables `hlig`, which is intended for old-fashioned ligatures."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:306
msgid "Contextual Alternates"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:306
msgid ""
"Enables `calt`, which is frequently used by script fonts and decorative "
"fonts to select appropriate glyphs depending on their context."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:310
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype-ligatures.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:310
msgid ""
"Ligatures in “Noto Serif” and “Junicode”, with the ligatures marked in blue, "
"and the lack of ligatures marked in orange. “ffi” is a common ligature in "
"Noto Serif, and contextual in Junicode, “st” is a discretionary ligature in "
"Junicode and “al” is a historical ligature in Junicode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:315
msgid "Glyphs: Position"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:317
msgid "Enable super or subscripts on the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:319
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:516
msgid "Super"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:320
msgid "Enables superscript glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:322
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:519
msgid "Sub"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:322
msgid "Enables subscript glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:326
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype-position.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:326
msgid "Showing sub and superscripts in the font “EB Garamond”."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:331
msgid "Glyphs: Numeric"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:333
msgid "Enable number-related glyph forms on the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:337
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:344
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:351
msgid "Does not explicitly enable either style, showing the font default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:338
msgid "Lining"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:339
msgid "Requests figures that fit within an upper case text, using `lnum`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:340
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:411
msgid "Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:340
msgid "Old Style"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:341
msgid ""
"Requests asks for figures that fit within an upper case text, using `onum`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:345
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:416
msgid "Proportional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:346
msgid "Requests proportional figures, using `pnum`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:347
msgid "Proportion"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:347
msgid "Tabular"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:348
msgid ""
"Requests tabular figures, using `tnum`, these figures all share the same "
"advance."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:352
msgid "Diagonal"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:353
msgid ""
"Replaces figures separated by a slash with a proper diagonal fraction form. "
"If a font has the numerator and denominator features, and the numbers are "
"separated by a 'fraction slash' (U+2044), then this will replace the figures "
"with numerators before the slash and denominators after the slash."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:354
msgid "Fraction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:354
msgid "Stacked"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:355
msgid "Replaces figures separated by a slash with a nut fraction form."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:356
msgid "Ordinals"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:357
msgid "Replaces letters that follow figures with their ordinal forms."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:359
msgid "Slashed Zero"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:359
msgid ""
"Replaces the number zero with one that has a slash in the middle, which can "
"help prevent confusion with similar glyphs like the letter 'O'."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:363
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype-numeric.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:363
msgid ""
"Showing numeric opentype features in the font “EB Garamond”. Selected is a "
"fraction “1/2”, beyond that it shows old style figures for “12345” in green, "
"tabular spacing for those old style figures in orange, and ordinals in blue."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:368
msgid "Glyphs: Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:370
msgid "Enable opentype features related to capitals, such as small caps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:373
msgid "Don't use any particular capitals."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:374
msgid "Small Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:375
msgid "Sets uppercase to small caps. Typically used for abbreviations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:376
msgid "All Small Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:377
msgid "Sets all text to small caps. Typically used for formal text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:378
msgid "Petite Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:379
msgid ""
"Sets uppercase to petite caps. Alternative to small caps that is exactly the "
"same as the x height."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:380
msgid "All Petite Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:381
msgid "Sets all text to petite caps."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:382
msgid "Titling Caps"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:383
msgid ""
"Sets uppercase to use titling caps. Titling caps frequently are larger and "
"more dramatic, and best suited for headers instead of body text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:385
msgid "Unicase"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:385
msgid "Enables the unicase feature."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:389
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype-caps.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:389
msgid ""
"Capital related opentype features in “EB Garamond” for small and petite "
"caps, “Estonia” for Titling caps and in a custom comic font for unicase "
"features."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:394
msgid "Glyphs: East-Asian"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:396
msgid "Enable glyph forms related to East Asian text layout."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:400
msgid "Use font default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:401
msgid "Traditional"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:402
msgid "Use traditional glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:403
msgid "Simplified"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:404
msgid "Use simplifies glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:405
msgid "JIS78"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:406
msgid "Use glyphs as specified by JIS78"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:407
msgid "JIS83"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:408
msgid "Use glyphs as specified by JIS83"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:409
msgid "JIS90"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:410
msgid "Use glyphs as specified by JIS90"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:411
msgid "JIS04"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:412
msgid "Use glyphs as specified by JIS04"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:414
msgid "Full Width"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:415
msgid "Use full width glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:417
msgid "Use proportional glyphs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:419
msgid "Ruby"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:419
msgid "Enable glyphs meant for ruby annotations."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:423
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/opentype-east-asian.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:423
msgid ""
"Showing the east-asian font variants in orange, using the font “Yu Gothic”. "
"Full-width is typically used for vertical text, JIS78 refers to a Japanese "
"industry standard that specifies certain glyph shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:428
msgid "Font Kerning"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:430
msgid ""
"Turn font kerning on or off. Font kerning enables per-glyph spacing "
"adjustments."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:436
msgid "Direction"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:438
msgid "Direction sets whether the text is left-to-right or right-to-left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:441
msgid "Unicode Bidi"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:442
msgid ""
"Unicode bidi gives extra control over how a shifted direction should be "
"interpreted. Typically the default algorithm is fine, but in some specific "
"cases, it cannot tell whether a sequence should be left-to-right or right-to-"
"left."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:445
msgid ""
"No controls are inserted. All text inside is reordered according to its "
"implicit direction (which is derived from the characters used)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:446
msgid "Embed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:447
msgid ""
"The sequence is directionally embedded. This means that the bidirectional "
"algorithm will assume the explicit direction is that of the :guilabel:"
"`direction` property, but the text itself is ordered by implicit direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:448
msgid "Override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:449
msgid ""
"Override means that the given section will use the current :guilabel:"
"`direction` as the explicit direction as well as the direction of the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:450
msgid "Isolate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:451
msgid ""
"Isolate controls are inserted. Isolate means that the bidirectional "
"algorithm treats the sequence as if it were a completely independent "
"paragraph. Due this, the ordering has no effect on the ordering of text on "
"either side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:452
msgid "Isolate-Override"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:453
msgid ""
"Both isolate and override are applied. This means that the text is ordered "
"explicitely by direction, but said ordering has no effect"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:455
msgid "Plain Text"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:455
msgid ""
":guilabel:`direction` property is unused and bididirectional algorithm will "
"instead guess at the direction."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:457
msgid ""
"Unicode bidi is one of the properties that does not inherit. The reason for "
"this is that it works by inserting bi directional algorithm controls at the "
"ends of the given range."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:462
msgid "Baseline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:464
msgid ""
"In some script traditions, the alignment point of text of different sizes "
"are different from the alignment point with Latin text. For compatibility "
"purposes, fonts of these scripts are usually made so the glyphs align "
"properly with Latin text. To achieve a more traditional alignment, dominant "
"and alignment baseline can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:466
msgid ""
"This feature will try to use data encoded in the fonts' baseline table. If "
"there's no such data, the baseline metrics will be auto-generated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:468
msgid "Dominant and Alignment baseline share the following options:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:470
msgid "Alphabetic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:471
msgid "Uses the baseline used by most scripts. Default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:472
msgid "Ideographic"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:473
msgid ""
"Uses the Ideographic design square and selects the bottom end in horizontal "
"mode, and the left side in vertical mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:474
msgid "Central"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:475
msgid ""
"Uses the Ideographic design square and selects the vertical center in "
"horizontal mode, and the horizontal center in vertical mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:476
msgid "Hanging"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:477
msgid "Align to the headstroke as used by North-Brahmic scripts."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:478
msgid "Middle"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:479
msgid ""
"Align to the center between the alphabetic baseline and x-height when laying "
"out horizontally, in vertical this is the central baseline."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:480
msgid "Mathematical"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:481
msgid "Align to the mathematical baseline, so that operator symbols align."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:482
msgid "Text Top"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:483
msgid "Align to the ascender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:485
msgid "Text Bottom"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:485
msgid "Align to the descender."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:490
msgid "Dominant Baseline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:494
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/baseline-example-devanagari.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:494
msgid ""
"In North Brahmic scripts like Devanagari, letters of different sizes align "
"at the headstroke. In the examples here, the top sample shows the default "
"behaviour, while the bottom sample uses :guilabel:`hanging` over the whole "
"text, which provides the traditional headstroke alignment."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:496
msgid ""
"Dominant Baseline specifies how stretches of text of different sizes are "
"aligned, it is also the default for :ref:`text_property_alignment_baseline`. "
"It has one unique value, :guilabel:`Auto`, which translates to :guilabel:"
"`Alphabetic` in horizontal and :guilabel:`Central` in vertical :ref:"
"`text_property_writing_mode`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:501
msgid "Alignment Baseline"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:503
msgid ""
"Alignment Baseline allows control over how this range of text is aligned to "
"the parent text. It has one unique property :guilabel:`Baseline`, which "
"means it will take its value from the :ref:`text_property_dominant_baseline` "
"property."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:505
msgid ""
"Alignment baseline does not inherit. Instead, child text will try to align "
"to the specified baseline of the parent text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:510
msgid "Baseline Shift"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:512
msgid ""
"Baseline shift allows moving the text away from the baseline, either by "
"predefined super and subscript values, or by a fixed amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:514
msgid "Length"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:515
msgid "Shift text by a specified amount."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:517
msgid ""
"Shift text so it aligns to the inherited super script offset. Said value is "
"retrieved from the font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:519
msgid ""
"Shift text so it aligns to the inherited sub script offset. Said value is "
"retrieved from the font."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:521
msgid ""
"Baseline shift does not inherit. Instead, shifts will be added to one "
"another, allowing the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:525
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/baseline-nested-super-script.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:525
msgid ""
"Nested baseline-shift super definitions. This is only possible by editing "
"the text with the SVG source editor."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:530
msgid "White Space"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:532
msgid ""
"The CSS white space rule controls how multiples of spaces are handled, and "
"whether the text can wrap."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:534
msgid "By default, this property is hidden."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:539
msgid "Language"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:541
msgid ""
"The language of this text shape. Language affects a number of properties, "
"like glyph shape, upper- and lowercase and line breaking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:543
msgid ""
"The text input allows typing any valid `BCP 47 <https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/BCP47>`_ code. Pressing :kbd:`enter` will cause Krita to parse the "
"code. Typing a language name or code into the text input will show a "
"filtered search pop-up."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:545
msgid ""
"Pressing on the down arrow will show all previously used locales this "
"session, as well as stored locales. By toggling the check box in front of a "
"locale, you can indicate that they need to be stored for future sessions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:547
msgid ""
"There is also a :guilabel:`Script` dropdown. Normally, it is possible to "
"guess the script from the language and country. However, in some places, "
"different scripts can be used for the same language, and sometimes the main "
"script being used has changed over the years. The script dropdown allows "
"setting the script in these cases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:552
msgid "Fill"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:554
msgid ""
"Fill can currently not be set with the text properties docker. You will need "
"to use the :ref:`shape_selection_tool` to set it on the paragraph, or change "
"the foreground color with any of the color selectors."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:559
msgid "Stroke"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:561
msgid ""
"Stroke can currently not be configured with the text properties docker. You "
"will need to use the :ref:`shape_selection_tool` to set it, or use the :ref:"
"`svg_source_editor` in the text tool to manually set a stroke."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:566
msgid "Paragraph Properties"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:568
msgid ""
"Paragraph properties are the properties that can only be applied over a "
"whole text shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:573
msgid "Writing Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:575
msgid ""
"Writing Mode sets whether the text flows horizontally or vertically, and in "
"the latter case, whether the block flows right-to-left or left-to-right."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:577
msgid "See also :ref:`text_property_direction`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:579
msgid ""
"A related feature is \"Text Orientation\", which allows rotating horizontal "
"text when it is typeset vertically. Krita does not current support this "
"feature, but it is planned in the future."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:584
msgid "Text Indent"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:586
msgid ""
"Text Indent allows setting indentation at the line start. Only works when "
"the text is wrapping. The main control is a slider defining the size of the "
"indent. There's two more advanced controls:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:588
msgid "Hanging Indentation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:589
msgid ""
"This does not apply indentation to the stating line, but instead the "
"subsequent lines."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:591
msgid "Indent after hard breaks"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:591
msgid ""
"This makes it so each line after a hard break qualifies as a starting lines. "
"Frequently used for poetry."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:596
#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:604
msgid "Text Align"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:598
msgid "Text Align sets the alignment for the given block of characters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:600
msgid ""
"The main control of this shows three buttons that correspond to start, "
"middle and end. These properties are affected by direction, meaning that for "
"right-to-left text, start will be the same as align right. The final button "
"is the justification toggle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:602
msgid "Opening the advanced settings shows the following:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:605
msgid ""
"This allows you to set the text alignment when text is wrapped in a shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:606
msgid "Align Last"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:607
msgid ""
"When :guilabel:`Text Align` is set to :guilabel:`Justified`, this controls "
"what to do with the final line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:609
msgid "Text Anchor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:609
msgid ""
"Text anchor controls how the text is anchored, instead of aligned. It "
"somewhat resembles :guilabel:`Text Align` in that it allows text to flow "
"from the left or right, but where :guilabel:`Text Align` is alignment within "
"a space, :guilabel:`Text Anchor` is relative to the starting point of the "
"text. You can use :guilabel:`Text Anchor` to set the anchor for each line, "
"as long as the text is not being auto wrapped."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:611
msgid ""
"This means that there's no justification for text that is not wrapped in "
"shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:613
msgid "By default, this property is always visible, even when not set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:618
msgid "Hanging Punctuation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:620
msgid ""
"Hanging punctuation allows hanging opening and closing punctuation as well "
"as commas. This implementation only implements East-Asian style hanging "
"punctuation."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:622
msgid "Hang first"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:623
msgid ""
"Opening punctuation such as opening quotes or opening brackets at the start "
"of the paragraph will be hung."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:624
msgid "Line end"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:625
msgid ""
"This toggle will allow or force commas and periods to hang at the end of any "
"line."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:627
msgid ""
"Closing punctuation such as closing quotes or closing brackets at the end of "
"the paragraph will be hung."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:628
msgid "Hang last"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:633
msgid "Tab Size"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:635
msgid ""
"Tab Size allows defining the size of tabulation characters. Tabulation "
"characters (inserted with :kbd:`tab`) are a type of white space that snaps "
"to the nearest multiple of the reference size. Its main use case is to align "
"columns of information without resorting to tables."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:637
msgid ""
"Tab size has one unique unit: :guilabel:`Sp`. This means the tab size uses "
"the current advance of the space character as unit."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:642
msgid "Text Rendering"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:644
msgid ""
"Text Rendering controls the hinting and rendering style for the text shape."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:646
msgid "Optimize Speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:647
msgid ""
"The hinting style for monochrome bitmaps is used, and anti-aliasing is "
"turned off. Krita will also take care to snap the glyphs to the nearest "
"pixel. This allows for pixel art fonts to look good, as well as being the "
"fastest to render option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:648
msgid "Optimize Legibility"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:649
msgid ""
"In vertical writing modes, full hinting is enabled, while for horizontal, "
"hinting only happens vertically. Krita will additionally snap relevant "
"metrics in these directions."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:650
msgid "Geometric Precision"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:651
msgid "No hinting is performed at all."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:653
msgid "Same as :guilabel:`Geometric Precision`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:657
msgid ".. image:: /images/text/unifont-text-rendering-example.png"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:657
msgid ""
"The Krita slogan in various scripts, typeset with the “Unifont” pixel font. "
"By using :guilabel:`Optimize Speed`, Krita knows to not just disable anti-"
"aliasing, but it will also try to snap the glyphs so that :ref:"
"`text_property_baseline_shift`, :ref:`text_property_letter_spacing` and :ref:"
"`text_property_line_height` will look good."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:662
msgid "Text Area"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:664
msgid "These properties are related to :ref:`text_in_shape`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:666
msgid "Shape Padding"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:667
msgid "This is the padding that is calculated on the Inside shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:669
msgid "Shape Margin"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:669
msgid ""
"This is margin around the \"Subtract\" shapes that is added before they are "
"removed from the \"Inside\" shapes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:674
msgid "Style Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:676
msgid ""
":ref:`resource_style_presets` allow storing combinations of properties for "
"later use. See that page for information about editing style presets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:678
msgid ""
"|mouseleft| an entry will select it for editing, while double |mouseleft| "
"will apply the active properties onto the text."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:680
msgid "The buttons at the bottom allow modifying the style presets:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:682
msgid "Import Style Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:683
msgid "Import an SVG with a style preset definition inside."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:684
msgid "Delete Style Presets"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:685
msgid "Disable a given style preset."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:686
msgid "Create Style Preset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:687
msgid "Creates a style preset from the current settings."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:688
msgid "Clone Preset"
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:689
msgid "Clones the current presets and shows the edit window."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:691
msgid "Edits the current selected presets."
msgstr ""

#: ../../reference_manual/dockers/text_properties.rst:693
msgid "Edit Preset"
msgstr ""
